<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76182" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχᾰ</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		Adv., used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only as intens. before the 
			Sup.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστος, ὄχ᾽ ἄριστος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>far</i> the best, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.69
			</span></i>, al.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξοχα</span>. (Prob.
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω</span> to hold; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχα</span> is to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχυρός</span> as the old <i><span class="en">
				Germ.
			</span></i>
			<i>fast</i> very, to <i>fest</i> fast, tight.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
